course: dictionary
lesson: 15132
title: Strong words, strong feelings
level: primary-5
stars: 3
explain: Some words show how strong something is. Savagery is a noun, a naming word for a thing. It names great cruelty or fierce wildness. «The savagery of the war shocked the whole town.» The sentence tells you the war was not just bad but brutal, so savagery means extreme cruelty.
explain: Look for clues around the word. «The lion's savagery as it attacked the zebra was shown in the film.» Nature films do not show gentle things. The word attacked is a clue that savagery means fierce, violent behaviour.
explain: Savagery comes from the describing word savage. «The savage storm tore off the roof.» Savage means fierce and wild. Adding -ry turns it into a naming word, so the savagery is the fierceness itself.
explain: Be careful with old books. Long ago, some writers used savage as an insulting word for people from other cultures. That was wrong and unkind. Today we use savagery only for cruel or fierce behaviour, never to describe people.
fact: Savagery is a noun, a word that names a thing or a quality.
fact: «Savagery» means very cruel and violent behaviour.
fact: «Savagery» can also mean fierce wildness, like the savagery of a storm.
fact: «Savage» is the describing word, and savagery is the naming word made from it.
fact: In old books, «savage» was sometimes used unkindly about people of other cultures. This was wrong, so do not use it that way.
exercise: «The savagery of the attack shocked everyone who saw the film.» What does savagery mean? | *Very cruel and violent behaviour | A kind and gentle offer | Quiet, peaceful calm | Loud, happy laughter
exercise: «The savagery of the storm tore off the roof.» Find and copy the naming word that means fierce wildness. | roof | *savagery | tore | storm
exercise: Mia says, «The savagery of the wolf pack chilled the hikers.» Which sentence uses savagery correctly? | The savagery of the birthday cake was delicious. | *The savagery of the wolf pack chilled the hikers. | The savagery of the kind teacher helped us read. | The savagery of the sunny beach made us smile.
test: «The war was full of savagery, and many families lost their homes.» What does savagery mean here? | *Great cruelty | Fast running | Quiet rest | Great fun
test: Which describing word is savagery made from? | *savage | sadness | silly | savagery
exam: Why should you not use «savage» to describe people from other cultures? | Because it is only used for animals in zoos | Because it means very clean | *Because it is an insulting word that was wrong and unkind | Because it is a noun
